# Store LF in the repository and check out LF in every working tree.
#
# The Docker image copies the working tree verbatim, and several build-time
# checks compare files byte-for-byte rather than logically. The
# paperclip-runner protocol manifest hashes its schema and fixture files with
# sha256, so a Windows checkout that turned those into CRLF failed the image
# build with "The generated PRP contract manifest is stale" even though nothing
# had actually changed.
#
# Pinning the eol here fixes that for every contributor and for CI. Setting
# core.autocrlf in a local git config cannot: it is per-machine, invisible to
# the next person, and the setting that caused the failure in the first place.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Patches are applied as text and must not gain or lose line endings.
patches/*.patch text eol=lf whitespace=-space-before-tab
